2025-10-08 12:28:59,981 [WARNING] Skipped idx=211: gold or llm supporting sentence is empty. gold='', llm='In the context of the provided information, the p73 gene, which is related to the p53 tumor suppressor, has been shown to be a target of the RARbeta/gamma-selective retinoid tazarotene. Tazarotene's mechanism of action includes the modulation of the p73 gene expression, specifically inducing the pro-apoptotic and anti-proliferative TAp73 isoforms while repressing the anti-apoptotic and pro-proliferative DeltaNp73 isoforms. This regulation occurs at the transcriptional level through its effects on the P1p73 and P2p73 promoters, which control the expression of the TAp73 and DeltaNp73 isoforms, respectively. The significance of p73 gene products in tazarotene-induced growth inhibition and their role in the treatment of skin tumors are highlighted, but the specific number of TAp73 isoforms identified in humans is not directly addressed. However, based on the existing knowledge, TAp73 refers to the full-length, pro-apoptotic isoform of p73, and there is no indication of multiple TAp73 isoforms. Therefore, the answer derived from this context is that one TAp73 isoform has been identified in humans.'
